title: Crates
summary: The workspace's crates, what each holds, and what each depends on.
order: 1
---

<script>
	import CrateMap from '$lib/components/CrateMap.svelte';
</script>

skoro is a workspace of five crates. Each depends only on the crates above it here, and a user
depends on `skoro`, which re-exports the core and the tensor layer, and on each feature crate a
model uses, such as `skoro-normal` and `skoro-spatial`. Each crate has a page of its own, which
says what it is for and gives the order in which to read its modules, computed from its sources when
the site is built: an order that uses as little as possible before it is read.

<CrateMap />

| crate          | what it holds                                                                                                                                            |
| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `skoro-tensor` | The layer over burn: the tensor shapes skoro computes with (`Points`, `Frame`, `Integers`, `Value`), each made at an explicit precision on a supported device, the `Target` that names them, host values, and the broadcasts and reshapes that carry values of no entries. |
| `skoro-core`   | Everything that makes a model a model: [spaces](../../concepts/spaces/) and typed handles, [operations](../../concepts/operations/) and their kernels, the writer and its [scopes](../../concepts/building/), [terms](../../concepts/terms/), [queries](../../concepts/queries/) and the compiler, embedded types, generation and retirement. |
| `skoro-normal` | The [normal distribution](../../concepts/the-normal/), on every space whose chart is global and whose volume is known: its term, its exact sampler, its scale in four forms, its roles, and the stacked tangent of a retirement's replacement, Gaussian or improper. |
| `skoro-spatial` | The [rotations and rigid motions](../../concepts/rotations-and-motions/): the unit quaternions, the rigid motions and the extended poses as embedded types with global charts and declared volumes, and their maps, from compositions and actions to exponentials, Jacobians, interpolations and Euler angles, as composites of the core's operations. |
| `skoro`        | The crate a user depends on: it re-exports `skoro-core`, and `skoro-tensor` as `skoro::tensor`, with `Device`, `Precision` and `Target` at its root.     |

The normal is the first distribution, and the rotations and rigid motions the first curved types.
What the core leaves for later entries (other distributions, spheres, linear algebra, least squares,
elimination, serialization and bindings among them)
is listed in the repository's
[`REVISIT.md`](https://github.com/mvarble/skoro/blob/main/REVISIT.md).
